  "body": "The spec uses \"an iframe element with a nested browsing context\", and \"the user agent must discard the nested browsing context, if any.\" Being pedantic, nothing really defines that the element not longer is \"an iframe element with a nested browsing context\" after the browsing context is discarded.\n\nIt might be clearer if the iframe had a \"nested browsing context\" that's either a browsing context or null.\n",
